STEP 1 — PACKET ALONE (answered before the master was read; Q5 before Q3 as ordered)

Q5. No. No sentence in the packet tells me any outcome is more consequential than any other, to the lane or to anyone. The only consequence-bearing sentences are: (i) packet line 251, "No tier, warrant token, standing or stamp moves. Published sources only; nothing from another lane. Paper HOLD; nothing outward." — a uniform freeze that equalises every outcome (nothing moves whatever the tally); and (ii) packet line 105, "INCONCLUSIVE, and it takes precedence over CENSUS_COMPLETE", with line 107-108's "The census is void" — procedural fates of the study itself, not consequences to any party, and not differentiating any per-claim outcome or tally content from any other. I tested the INCONCLUSIVE label adversarially for a steering channel (a seat nudging marginal claims into the arithmetic group to make the census "conclusive"); the filing rules are mechanical, precedence-bound, dual-seated and audited, so the channel has no filing to act on. CONSEQUENCE_VISIBLE=NO.

Q3. From the packet alone I CAN infer the following, each with the leaking sentence:
 (a) The lane's comparison structure is a per-claim provenance dichotomy — packet line 15: "what does that number rest on — derived and standard inputs only, or a chosen, fitted, imported or undeclared one?" There is a clean pole and a suspect pole; the census is built to sort claims between them. (The origin enum at packet line 149 adds MEASURED, which neither pole of the dichotomy names — see §6, cosmetic finding.)
 (b) The corpus is cosmology and the standard pole is the Planck 2018 baseline — packet lines 185/196: the closed STANDARD list (H₀, Ω_m, Ω_Λ, Ω_b h², Ω_c h², n_s, σ₈, τ, ln(10¹⁰ A_s), age) and "The cosmological rows are the Planck 2018 TT,TE,EE+lowE+lensing baseline."
 (c) The lane expects chosen/fitted inputs and fought to keep them reproducible — packet line 41-43: "*(V10, option (c): refusing chosen inputs stopped this being reproduction at all — a paper can direct you to use its own chosen constant, and following that instruction IS reproducing the paper.)*" and packet line 51: "**One pass, two tallies (option (c), the principal's ruling 2026-09-05).**" The design iterated at least ten versions and its contested core was chosen-input admissibility, settled by a ruling. The stake I reconstruct: the lane wants "reproduces while resting on chosen/fitted/imported values" to be a reportable combination — the interest lives in the rests_on tally, not the verdict tally.
 (d) Clean-looking provenance is valued by someone — packet line 166: "A chain cannot be made to look clean by classifying only its last step." There is a "clean" and a "not clean" look, and the machinery anticipates someone wanting the clean look.
 (e) A hidden pattern exists and the seat is deliberately blinded to it — the control token at packet lines 202/204: "C4_PATTERN_BLIND". Existence only; no content, no polarity.
 (f) Provenance carries consequence for outcomes decided elsewhere — packet line 173-174: "*(What `root_origins` implies for a claim's outcome follows from the clause held in §3 and is not decided here; the field is factual either way.)*" The sentence asserts an implication from root_origins to a claim's outcome while pointing at a clause the seat cannot see (and that contradicts packet line 16, "Neither contaminates the other").
 (g) The lane hopes the census is conclusive — packet line 105 labels CENSUS_PARTIAL "INCONCLUSIVE", making CENSUS_COMPLETE the only conclusive study outcome.
 What I CANNOT infer from the packet: the hypothesis's content, the comparison model's identity (no occurrence of any model name), the rests_on value set or severity order (not printed in the packet), what the interpretation does with the tallies, and — decisively — which direction of tally the lane hopes for. The packet hands me the field the lane watches (provenance purity) but not the bet it placed.

STEP 2 — THE OPERATIVE SECTIONS JUDGED (1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,11; §10 read in full, binds nothing)

1. OUTCOME CLASSES

Per-claim (six classes + total precedence). Exhaustive and mutually exclusive EXCEPT at one constructible boundary — the one real defect this gate found:

R1 (DECIDABILITY GAP, NOT COSMETIC). Constructed case: a paper prints claim M, states equation E producing it, and E needs input σ. The paper does not print σ but writes "we use the velocity dispersion from Paper B [37]" — and Paper B is itself one of the 89 pinned enumerable texts sitting in the seat's working directory (the corpus pins, e.g., a Planck-2018 text that other corpus papers plausibly cite for needed values). Trace: σ is not PRINTED ("given in the paper" — it is not), not STANDARD, so by §2 step 3 it is ABSENT; §2 (packet line 46): "**A seat may not supply a value for an `ABSENT` input.** Encountering one ends that claim's attempt." Now file the outcome. Not REPRO_NO_DERIVATION_STATED (an equation is stated). Not REPRO_BLOCKED — packet line 72-73: "an input whose value the paper does not print, but for which the paper **names a source (a citation)**, where that source is outside this lane and cannot be obtained" — the source is inside the lane and obtainable. Not REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT — packet line 82-83: "**neither printed nor traced to any named source**" — it IS traced to a named source. Not REPRO_NOT_EVALUABLE (no arithmetic ran; the attempt ended). Not the arithmetic group (no attempt). So the claim satisfies no class, and packet line 85 "**Exactly one outcome is filed per claim**" cannot be satisfied; the claim also cannot "carry" the non-arithmetic outcome CENSUS_PARTIAL requires (packet line 103). The BLOCKED/ABSENT boundary leaves "named source, obtainable" with a status but no outcome.
  Verbatim quotes: above. Exact replacement (one clause added to §2 step 3, master line 72-73 / packet line 37-38): "**A value the paper does not print but traces to a named source that is itself a pinned enumerable text is classified `PRINTED` from that source, with `origin` `IMPORTED`, `origin_evidence` `ORIG_CITATION` cited to the named source's file and line, and the value machine-matched there.**" The attempt then proceeds, the claim files REPRO_EXACT or REPRO_FAILED with rests_on reflecting IMPORTED, and REPRO_BLOCKED keeps its exclusive domain (named source outside the lane / unobtainable). Consistent with §11 (the pinned corpus is the lane's published sources) and C4 (the pinned sources are in the working directory).

Otherwise the per-claim system is total: any claim either states no procedure (NO_DERIVATION_STATED), or has an untraced missing input (INPUT_ABSENT), or a traced-unobtainable one (BLOCKED), or all inputs present — then the 120-second cap / machinery limit (NOT_EVALUABLE) or a completed attempt decides EXACT vs FAILED mechanically by the stated-precision rounding rule (packet line 64-67). A claim fitting TWO outcomes is constructible (their own example: an absent input whose source is also unobtainable satisfies BLOCKED and INPUT_ABSENT) and the stated total precedence files exactly one. ✓

Study-level (seven classes + total precedence, chronological). A tally fitting two classes: a control split co-occurring with a denominator dispute files CENSUS_CONTROL_SPLIT by the stated order (packet line 119-121); ORIGIN_DISPUTED + AUDIT_FAILED files CENSUS_ORIGIN_DISPUTED. A tally fitting none: none constructible — every terminal configuration satisfies at least one class. INCONCLUSIVE is genuinely reachable: one ABSENT input anywhere in the 106,676-line corpus files REPRO_INPUT_ABSENT, and CENSUS_PARTIAL takes precedence over CENSUS_COMPLETE by its own clause. ✓

Q1 (direct): Does §3's definition, as written under option (c), make every declared outcome reachable and keep the reproduction question decidable? Reachability: YES — all six per-claim outcomes and all seven study-level classes have constructible inputs (the retired-class defect of prior rounds is gone; the arithmetic group of exactly two members is enterable by any fully-stated claim). Decidability: YES on every hardest case I constructed — except the R1 boundary case above, where it is NO until repaired. Required traces:
  - Printed-but-chosen input (β-style, "We take the coupling beta = 0.001076 for the model."): status PRINTED, origin CHOSEN (ORIG_CHOICE_STATED, verbatim machine-matched); §2 step 4 consumes it ("chosen and fitted values included"); arithmetic runs; files REPRO_EXACT if the reproduced value rounds to the printed numeral at stated precision, else REPRO_FAILED; the pinned script computes rests_on=USES_CHOSEN — machine-verified: `compute` on my synthetic ledger printed "cB\trests_on=USES_CHOSEN\troot_origins=['CHOSEN']". Exactly one outcome, exactly one rests_on.
  - Fitted parameter the paper states ("Our fit gives n_s = 0.9649"): PRINTED + FITTED, consumed, EXACT/FAILED, rests_on=USES_FITTED (severity rungs machine-verified: {IMPORTED,CHOSEN}→USES_IMPORTED, {FITTED,UNDECLARED}→USES_UNDECLARED).
  - Imported value ("We adopt H0 = 67.4 from Planck (2018)."): the reason-code precedence ("a sentence that names an external source for the value is a citation whatever else it says") files ORIG_CITATION→IMPORTED; PRINTED status consumed; EXACT/FAILED; rests_on=USES_IMPORTED (machine-verified: "cC\trests_on=USES_IMPORTED\troot_origins=['CHOSEN', 'IMPORTED']").
  - Stated-precision boundary: a claim printed "13.8 Gyr" with recipe output 13.797 files REPRO_EXACT by the printed-precision rounding clause — the V10 ambiguity is mechanically dead.
  The option-(c) architecture resolves the four-round tension: the verdict never filters on provenance, and provenance is never computed by a seat. The residual is R1 — a one-clause totality repair, not the tension returning.

2. CONTROLS

Each control names an exact code; C1/C2/C3/C5/C5b/C6 carry PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN; C4 carries PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN for the seat instruction and C4_PACKET_REDACTED lane-side. Unreached controls: "Controls in an unreached limb are `NOT_RUN`, never passes." (packet line 230) ✓. No control can be passed by bare assertion: C0 requires two independent seats' printed exhibition tables; C1/C2/C3 require the pinned script's exit 0 with command/stdout/exit printed; C5 requires live execution (transcription fails by construction); C4/C5b are self-reported path lists — and C4 says so itself ("This is procedural, not enforced by the filesystem… a self-reported control with a structural aid, and is labelled so", master line 287-289). C5b carries the same mechanism without the same honesty label; COSMETIC (same family, already covered by C4's admission).
  C0's operative line ends "`C0_REACHABILITY=PASS`." (packet line 135 / master line 195) with no FAIL|NOT_RUN form, while §10.5 claims "every control `PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN`" was applied. COSMETIC — C0 is pre-freeze, its fail state is defined by the freeze block; changes no passability. Exact replacement: "`C0_REACHABILITY=PASS|FAIL|NOT_RUN`."

Q2 (direct): Is the provenance field checkable rather than asserted? Tested by execution against the pinned script, not read off the text:
  - Fabricated quotation: record citing verbatim "we chose beta = 0.001076" against a line that does not contain it → `validate` printed "FAIL: in_b: verbatim not found at paperA.txt:1", exit 1. The machine catches it. ✓
  - Value not at the cited line: "FAIL: in_b: value 0.999 not at cited line", exit 1. ✓
  - Schema fields: an ABSENT record missing value/source_file/source_line → "FAIL: in_z: missing ['value', 'source_file', 'source_line']". ✓
  - THE REQUIRED TEST — wrong-but-plausible origin: source line "We adopt H0 = 67.4 from Planck (2018)." cited with reason_code ORIG_CHOICE_STATED (the stated precedence requires ORIG_CITATION: "a sentence that names an external source for the value is a citation whatever else it says") and a correctly machine-matched quotation → `validate` printed "C3_NO_SUBSTITUTION=PASS", exit 0. THE MACHINE DOES NOT CATCH IT. The reason-code precedence is seat discipline, not machine-enforced. What catches it as written: (i) the second seat's independent classification — a divergent code lands in `origin_alt` and the claim's rests_on is computed under both and marked DISPUTED (machine-verified: `compute` printed "c1\trests_on=['USES_CHOSEN', 'USES_IMPORTED']\troot_origins=['CHOSEN']\tDISPUTED"), so the misclassification becomes visible rather than silent; (ii) the C6 auditor, who "re-classifies every input's `origin` from the pinned sources" without sight of earlier work. If all readers make the same plausible error, no mechanism catches it — that is the judgement floor, and the document states floors for the blind and the seal but not this one. Answer to Q2: the citation envelope (quotation + value) is machine-checked, the computation (root_origins, rests_on, seat-written rejection) is machine-checked — verified exit 2 on both pre-set fields — but the reason-code choice inside a correctly matched quotation is asserted; the catching mechanism is redundancy (second seat + auditor), never a machine check. As the brief anticipates: that is the answer.
  Exact repair (one sentence appended to C3, master line 232-233 / packet line 161-162): "**A reason code that matches its quotation but misapplies the precedence is caught only by the second seat's independent classification and the C6 re-classification, never by the machine; if every reader misclassifies identically, the record stands — the record states this floor rather than implying a machine check of judgement.**"
  Also verified: the script FAILS (exit 1) a dangling derived_from ("derived_from ghost_input not in ledger"), a cycle ("cycle at x1"), and a DERIVED record with no derived_from — the three laundering guards behave exactly as C3 claims; transitive roots computed to depth 2 (verified); "an empty root set cannot occur" holds as written.

3. CIRCULARITY

Inclusion: the §1 rule is mechanical in form ("prints a numeral the paper asserts as a result of its own" plus five enumerated excluded kinds), applied independently by two seats with tolerance zero — any disagreement stops the study under CENSUS_DENOMINATOR_DISPUTED, so a contested exclusion cannot pass silently; it stops the census rather than hiding the claim. Exclusions are not outcomes: every excluded candidate is recorded with file, line, numeral and kind, and the third seat "first audits the full candidate and exclusion ledgers against every pinned source — completeness, not just outcomes" (packet line 210-211). To quietly exclude a contrary claim it must vanish from both independent enumerations AND from the completeness audit. I cannot construct that path short of three independent readers failing identically.
  Origin classification: cited, machine-matched, dual, never reconciled, dispute carried as a printed pair — the lane's preference cannot settle a classification, only record it or stop the study (>10% → CENSUS_ORIGIN_DISPUTED).
  Interpretation: the hypothesis touches the tally exactly once, after the two-receipt seal, via a protocol committed and receipted BEFORE limb A, which no seat may open, and which reads "the ledger's `rests_on` tally and the reproduction tally as two separate facts" — the only content §7 states.
  Residual channels that remain open (they inform the seat where the lane's interest lives; none can reach a filing): the §1 dichotomy framing (packet line 15); the "look clean" valence (packet line 166); the stale implication parenthetical (packet line 173-174, R3 below); the C4_PATTERN_BLIND token (R2 below); the version/ruling residue (R4 below). Filings are mechanical, precedence-bound, dual and audited, so these inform but cannot steer — but R2/R3/R4 are exactly the leak family this gate was ordered to hunt, and all three are one-clause repairs.
  The exclusion kind "attributed-not-derived" requires a judgement (attributed vs derived); bounded by the same zero-tolerance duality and audit. Noted; no repair needed.

