5. THE SEAL (§7)

Sound as written. (P) binds the interpretation protocol — hash and commit id, receipted and timestamped by Blanc, outside the lane — BEFORE limb A begins, and "limb A does not begin without receipt P": since no tally can exist before limb B, the protocol cannot be written to suit the tally. (T) binds the tally after it is committed and before the protocol is opened: "the interpretation protocol is not opened without both receipts." After opening, Blanc independently re-hashes BOTH artefacts and verifies all four values against the two receipts; the interpretation report must print both receipts and the four verified values; any missing receipt or mismatch files CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED — and §4 item 3's definition names exactly that case ("or the §7 receipt verification fails", packet line 107-108) ✓. The local commit is correctly demoted ("tamper evidence, not an external custodian"), and the residual is stated without overclaim: "It does not prove Tori had not already guessed the answer — nothing available here could prove that. It bounds the record, not the mind." The relay binds what it claims to bind, before the step it must precede. Verified as delivered: R3C2_INTERPRETATION_PROTOCOL_20260904.md exists on disk, so "lives in" is presently true; receipt P is what binds its future form. Operational caveat, not a design defect: nothing binds the custodian's availability.

6. FAIRNESS

The negative outcome carries the mandated wording: "**Wording: "unreproduced from the stated inputs," not "error."**" (packet line 70) ✓; the C6 audit text contains no "error" ("Any outcome the audit cannot reproduce… files CENSUS_AUDIT_FAILED") ✓. No study-level class asserts more than its definition: CENSUS_COMPLETE is defined over the arithmetic group with the exclusion ledger reported alongside; "INCONCLUSIVE" accurately describes a partial census; "The census is void" accurately describes an audit/seal failure. Two name/prose frictions:
  - The NAME `REPRO_EXACT` asserts exact equality while the class admits within-stated-precision matches (packet line 64-67). The definition governs every filing, so this changes no class filed — COSMETIC; §10.5 already escalates the rename to the principal, where it belongs.
  - The §1 dichotomy (packet line 15) names the clean pole "derived and standard inputs only" while the computed field's clean pole is derived + standard + MEASURED (machine-verified: roots ['MEASURED'] → rests_on=DERIVED_ONLY). The question prose understates the field it introduces; the field itself is script-computed, so no filing changes — COSMETIC. Exact replacement: "(ii) what does that number rest on — derived, standard or measured inputs only, or a chosen, fitted, imported or undeclared one?"

